--TEST--
A Core\Cli\Progress handle refuses to advance once the bar it names has closed -- ADR 0086 sections 5 and 8
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The same scoping `Core\Cli\Live` has, said in this member's own words: a bar
// ends with the `Core\Cli::progress` call that drew it, so a handle answered
// out of that call names a region that is no longer there.
var $escaped = Core\Cli::progress(3, fn(Core\Cli\Progress $bar): Core\Cli\Progress => {
    $bar->advance({label: "while it is open"});
    return $bar;
});
try {
    $escaped->advance();
    echo "advanced\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo $e->message, "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
Core\Cli\Progress::advance(): this handle's region has closed, or an inner one is open inside it — a progress bar is scoped to the `Core\Cli::progress` call that made it, and only the innermost open region paints
